Network Monitoring, Security and Auditing — Blue Team Project

Student: AIKINS BISMARK
Index number: FCM.41.018.027.23
Course: CY376: NETWORK MONITORING, SECURITY AND AUDITING
Team: Blue Team
Supervisor / Instructor: TBD
Date: 03 August 2026

Abstract

This project explores practical Blue Team techniques for network monitoring, security, and auditing within a controlled lab environment. Over a month I built a small instrumented network using Python-based packet capture tools, simulated benign and adversarial activity, and applied rule-based detection and logging to evaluate coverage. The work focused on (1) establishing visibility by capturing packets and flows, (2) centralized logging and correlation of host/network events, and (3) evaluating detection efficacy and tuning to reduce false positives. Using custom Python scripts (packet_sniffer.py) for capture and analysis, I detected reconnaissance activity (port scans) and active manipulation attempts (ARP spoofing). The report documents lab design and configuration, implementation excerpts (code and configuration), results (logs and alerts), analysis mapped to MITRE ATT&CK techniques, and prioritized recommendations to improve monitoring, retention, alerting, and incident response. The appendices contain full scripts and full logs.

